linux-drm for air/OS: licensing
===============================

This repository holds code under more than one licence.

linux/
    The sources of Linux 6.18.52 this port compiles, imported unchanged
    (tools/import-linux.sh). The few files the port changed afterwards say so
    after their licence block, and the changes are in the git history. Every
    file keeps its own licence, named by its SPDX-License-Identifier line or
    written out in its header: most of DRM and amdgpu is MIT, TTM is
    GPL-2.0 OR MIT, and dma-buf, parts of the DRM core and the library code
    are GPL-2.0. The licence texts are in linux/LICENSES; a file without a
    licence statement is under the GPL-2.0, as linux/COPYING says.

haiku/, tools/
    The Linux kernel API on Haiku (haiku/compat), the Haiku driver
    (haiku/amdgpu), tests and build and packaging tools, written for air/OS:
    the MIT licence below, unless a file says otherwise
    (haiku/compat/include/linux/string.h is GPL-2.0).

The amdgpu_drm kernel add-on
    Built from both, it is a combined work distributed under the GNU General
    Public License, version 2 (linux/LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0). This
    repository is its complete source; haiku/build/Makefile builds it.

Firmware
    This repository holds no firmware. The amdgpu_firmwares package that
    haiku/tools/package.sh makes carries the amdgpu files of linux-firmware
    unchanged, under their own licence (LICENSE.amdgpu, which the package
    installs as "AMD GPU Firmware").


